{
  "title": "Unknown tool NAME aborts the game; unknown tool ARGUMENTS are dropped in \
silence",
  "description": "The two ends of the same dispatch decision behave in opposite and \
equally unhelpful ways. A tool call naming a tool that is not registered raises a fatal \
error and the harness ABORTS THE GAME: the pilot exits code 1, the launcher records the \
generic exit reason 'launch exited', and the episode is lost. A tool call naming a \
REGISTERED tool but passing arguments the tool does not declare has those arguments \
dropped without a word (issue 46512add, filed 2026-09-03). One direction destroys the \
episode over a recoverable mistake; the other conceals a real defect. \
\
MEASURED 2026-09-04 on ranokau, D-gate leg1 config, 20 games per policy, three games lost \
across 40: Eval08 called 'Choose_action' (registered: 'choose_action' -- a capitalisation), \
Eval09 called 'get_active_choices' and Eval14 called 'get_game_action_choices' (registered: \
'get_action_choices'). All three are near-misses of a real tool name. There were ZERO \
non-fatal instances: every unknown tool call killed its game. \
\
WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THE LOST GAMES. The failure is indistinguishable from \
infrastructure at every layer above it. The per-game exit reason is 'launch exited', the \
same string written when a launch genuinely dies, and the cause appears only in the game's \
errors.log. A model-behaviour regression therefore presents as a machine fault and is \
counted as one: an OPD evaluation on 2026-09-04 reported these games as infrastructure \
failures and explicitly advised against attributing them to the policy, which inverted the \
night's conclusion until the errors.log was read. Rates across a training trajectory were \
0/20, 1/20, 2/20 -- a signal that was invisible while it wore an infrastructure label. \
\
DESCRIBING, NOT PROPOSING A FIX. Any change here alters what an in-flight evaluation \
measures, and the defect must stay in place to be measured. Worth deciding deliberately: \
whether an unregistered name should return a tool error to the model (which can retry, as \
it can for any other bad call) rather than ending the episode; whether unknown arguments \
should be an error rather than silently dropped; and separately, that the exit reason \
recorded for an aborted game should name the abort's cause rather than reuse the string \
for a dead launch.",
